From 3e24712fd128fa2c6f30c00fee6b51a8c54e45c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:58:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Generic test of the linear solvers on the linear elasticity

LinearSolverFactoriesTest --elasticity solves a cantilever beam in linear
elasticity (three components per node) with each linear solver and each
preconditioner given to GMRES, sequential and parallel, on the CPU and on
a CUDA GPU (the parallel variant on the GPU, which lasts eight minutes,
is not registered). On this problem, a converged resolution must have a
residual lower than 1e-6 (GMRES stops on the preconditioned residual,
a few hundred times smaller than the residual for the incomplete
factorizations), and the entries which do not converge with the options
of the test are listed with the reason: conjugate gradient squared with
a Jacobi preconditioner (divergence for Ginkgo, breakdown for MAGMA),
stationary iterations with a damped Jacobi preconditioner (too slow),
pipelined conjugate gradient of Ginkgo (stagnation on the GPU), TFQMR of
MAGMA (breakdown), multigrid of Ginkgo (aggregation without the rigid
body modes); for them, only the report of the convergence is checked.
The approximate solvers (one cycle of a scalar algebraic multigrid) are
only required to give a finite residual. The residuals are printed in
scientific notation.
---
 tests/CMakeLists.txt                |  17 +++-
 tests/LinearSolverFactoriesTest.cxx | 139 +++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 129 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

